  "originalQuery": "You are a Database Engineer responsible for migrating a Cassandra database to Google Cloud Bigtable while ensuring minimal downtime and maintaining a fallback plan. Which of the following migration strategies is best for this scenario?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Develop custom scripts to convert the Cassandra schema to Bigtable and transfer the data using Bigtable APIs, then create a reverse replication process from Bigtable to the on-premises Cassandra database as a fallback plan.<br/>B. Use Cloud Data Fusion to convert the Cassandra schema and transfer the data to Bigtable, then create a Cloud Data Fusion pipeline to transfer the data back to the on-premises database as a fallback plan.<br/>C. Create a Bigtable instance, use Bigtable's import functionality to convert the schema and transfer data, and set up a reverse replication from Bigtable to the on-premises Cassandra database as a fallback.<br/>D. Utilize the Schema Conversion Tool (SCT) to convert the Cassandra schema for Bigtable, perform data transfer using Dataflow, and set up a reverse replication from Bigtable to the on-premises Cassandra database as a fallback.",
